# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  SecretBeans starter rules - credit-card exports
#
#  Written by Claude (Anthropic) with Edwin West, August 2026.
#  Not an Anthropic product. See PROVENANCE.md.
#
#  This template has only been tried against Chase exports. Check 'fields'
#  against your own CSV's column order before trusting anything it produces.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Starter rules for a credit-card export.

skip 1
fields  date, postdate, description, category, type, amount, memo
date-format %-m/%-d/%Y
currency $

account1 liabilities:creditcard:CHANGEME

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Categories. Later blocks win, so general first, specific after.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# if %description STOP.*SHOP
#   account2 expenses:food:groceries

# Some exports HTML-escape merchant names, so '&' arrives as '&amp;'.
# if %description STOP &amp; SHOP
#   description STOP & SHOP

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Payments to this card - see docs/TRANSFERS.md
#
# The payment also appears on the bank statement. The card side is the better
# owner because it knows which card was paid, so record it here and skip it in
# the bank's rules file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

if %description Payment Thank You
  account2 assets:bank:CHANGEME
